Note = {2nd International Conference on Advanced Science and Information
   Technology (ASCIT), Cheonan, SOUTH KOREA, MAY 12-13, 2017},
Abstract = {In this research, we investigated the distribution of donation behavior
   types among Korean people by dividing them into donation persistence
   group, donation intention group, donation discontinuation group, and
   persistent non-donation group. We also investigated what factors affect
   the types of donation behavior. Specifically, we examined the effects of
   donors' sharing behavior experience (e.g., service experience, periodic
   service experience, service experience in the last year, service
   intention within the next year), donors' donation internal/external
   motives, donors' recognition of donation organizations (e.g., awareness
   of donor organization, cognitive pathways to donor organization, key
   considerations in selecting donor agencies), donors' perceptions of
   donation organizations' transparency (e.g., importance of information
   disclosure by donor organization, opinion on strengthening regulation of
   donor organization, awareness of information disclosure by donor
   organization, etc.) on the types of donation behaviors and explored the
   social efforts to increase the size of high donation loyalty groups and
   to activate their loyalty.},
