Note = {22nd Congress of the International Ergonomics Association-IEA, SOUTH
   KOREA, AUG 25-29, 2024},
Abstract = {Intelligent companion robots provide emotional support, health
   monitoring, and assistance with daily activities, significantly
   enhancing the quality of life and psychological well-being of the
   elderly. This paper aims to construct a conceptual model of the
   relationship between user perception, individual characteristics, and
   the intention to use intelligent companion robots, based on the
   Technology Acceptance Model (TAM) and Technology Readiness Index (TRI)
   theory. Research hypotheses are proposed, and data is collected through
   online and offline questionnaires. Hypotheses are tested using
   structural equation modeling and PLS-SEM software to study the intention
   of the elderly to use companion robots. The study finds that: (1)
   Perceived value and technology readiness directly influence user
   intention. (2) Perceived value mediates the relationship between
   technology readiness and user intention. (3) TAM is one of the most
   explanatory models for understanding and predicting users' acceptance
   behaviors and intentions regarding information technology, although
   necessary modifications and improvements are needed due to its scope of
   application.},
