Abstract = {The construction process and its activities expose primarily supervisors
   and workers to: asbestos, dusts including silica and lead, chemicals,
   sunlight, diesel engine exhaust emissions; frequent loud noise; frequent
   or excessive use of vibrating tools; frequent or excessive manual
   handling of loads, and stress and fatigue. Registered professional
   construction health and safety agents (CHSAs) were surveyed to determine
   their OH perceptions. Key findings include: OH can be influenced during
   the six stages of projects, and 36 aspects/interventions have potential
   to improve construction OH. It is concluded that all parties can
   influence OH during the six stages of projects, although to varying
   degrees, due to differing degrees of participation in the respective
   stages, and 36 aspects/interventions can improve OH. It is recommended
   that all parties, clients, construction project managers, H\&S
   practitioners, designers, and contractors, including their managers,
   supervisors, and workers are educated and/or trained in terms of OH.
   Therefore, all built environment professionals' education and
   construction skills training should address OH.},
