Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {Agriculture education programs in Malaysian Schools were introduced to
   prepare human resource for Malaysia's agriculture sector. Agricultural
   programs relevant to jobs are offered in schools to ensure agricultural
   students are ready to choose a career in the agriculture sectors.
   However, several issues have emerged concerning career development in
   adolescents are. Career development among adolescents is always
   influenced by significant people around them. The aim of this paper is
   to discuss the influence of parents' ethnicity on agricultural students'
   career choice based on the theory of reason action. According to the
   theory, beside a person's attitude (positive or negative) the behavior
   towards performing particular behavior (e.g., choosing a career path) is
   affected by the perception of significant people around us (e.g.,
   parents, spouse, teachers, etc.). This is known as a person's normative
   belief. Logistic regression found significant differences in students'
   normative beliefs (mother and father) in choosing agriculture as a
   career according to their parents' ethnicity.},
