   PREVENTION},
Series = {INTERNATIONAL CONGRESS SERIES},
Year = {1999},
Volume = {1189},
Pages = {305-310},
Note = {1st International Conference on the History of Occupational and
   Environmental Prevention, PONTIFCIA UNIV URBANIANA, ROME, ITALY, OCT
   04-06, 1998},
Organization = {Ist Superiore Prevenz \& Sicurezza Lavoro; Milan Univ, Lavoro Luigi
   Devoto Clin; Inhoep; ICOH, Sci Comm Hist Prevent Occupat \& Environm Dis},
Abstract = {The relationship between the prevention of accidents and work-related
   illnesses and education had already been identified and subsequently
   highlighted by important public health and work physicians. From the mid
   19th century onwards, scholars began to highlight the effect of child
   labour on the family budget, but failed to realise the fundamental fact
   that education could contribute to an anthropological transformation
   with regard to social and productive organisation, social aggregation,
   social habits and social perception. In Italy, the right to health and
   education was recognized by the constitution of the republic, although
   these principles remained practically unheeded for many pears. It was
   only in the late 1960s, when an active movement came into being which,
   on the one hand involved the workers, their political organizations,
   their unions, and on the other researchers in different disciplines,
   that the issues of health and safety in the workplace were again put
   forward, also in culturally innovative and no longer exclusively
   naturalistic terms linked to clinical experiences.},
