   Application Technology (ESIAT 2009), Wuhan, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUL 04-05,
   2009},
Organization = {Intelligent Informat Technol Applicat Res Assoc; Indt Geodesy \&
   Geophys; Chinese Acad Sci; Engn Technol Press},
Abstract = {Image fusion is the process of generating a single combined image, which
   contains a more accurate description of the scene than the multiple
   images from different sources. Many approaches have been developed for
   the combination of complementary information coming from input images in
   order to create a new image where the informative content is more
   suitable for human visual or machine perception. Nonsubsampled
   Contourlet Transform (NSCT) can realize a flexible multiscale,
   multidirection, and shift-invariant image decomposition. As a result,
   when NSCT is introduced to image fusion, more information and better
   characteristics from the original images for fusion could be obtained.
   In this paper, NSCT is proposed when different registered source images
   are decomposed. Then with two distinct modes of fusion method in
   low-frequency and in high-frequency separately, the fused image will be
   obtained by inverse NSCT. Compared with the fusion method based on
   wavelet and other fusion methods, the experiments show that this
   approach can achieve better results than them.},
