   Acad Exchange Service Fdn; German Embassy},
Abstract = {The economy of Prince Edward County has been based largely on
   agricultural products, their processing and industries like shipbuilding
   which facilitate their export. A decline in these sectors has forced
   local government to contemplate alternative strategies, ideally those
   that capitalize on the region's natural and human resource heritage. One
   outcome has been considerable investment in the development of a
   substantial infrastructure to market culinary tourism products through
   sophisticated publications and websites. Taste the County is one of the
   most important initiatives, partnering to create a wide variety of
   tourism products, including the Taste Trail and numerous events that are
   held throughout the region. The establishment of twelve fully
   operational wineries contributes strongly to the culinary image that is
   sought and represents a base for further development of viticulture.
   Despite the array of culinary opportunities, the question remains about
   their success in attracting visitors. Using a survey of visitors, this
   study investigates their motivations to visit Prince Edward County,
   their behaviors and perceptions of the culinary experience.},
