   MONDUZZI EDITIORE},
Title = {Development of a risk assessment scale for HIV prevention among Thai
   army conscripts},
Booktitle = {XIV INTERNATIONAL AIDS CONFERENCE: PREVENTION SCIENCE},
Year = {2002},
Pages = {223-226},
Note = {14th International AIDS Conference, BARCELONA, SPAIN, JUL 07-12, 2002},
Organization = {Univ N Carolina; Gen Clin Res Ctr; UNC Ctr AIDS Res; Natl Inst Hlth;
   Swiss Natl AIDS Res Program; Bristol-Myers Squibb Co; Boehringer
   Ingelheim; GlaxoWellcome Res \& Dev, HIV Antiviral Res},
Abstract = {AIDS is a major public health problem of Thailand. Thai army conscripts
   are vulnerable for contracting HIV. This study was aimed to develop an
   instrument to identify who are at high risk for preventive intervention.
   A case control study was conducted among 240 HIV positive and 240 HIV
   negative conscripts. The variables found to be predictive of HIV
   seropositivity were: income more than 2000 Baht/month, heroin use, drug
   use before sex, first sex with female sex workers(FSWs), HIV risk
   perception and unworrying about HIV. The odds ratios from the analysis
   were used to develop the HIV risk assessment scale model by applying
   Receiver Operating Characteristic(ROC) curve analysis. With the cut-off
   point of 5.5 for HIV positive prediction, the sensitivity was 57.1 \%
   and the specificity was 78.8 \%. It was also be tested in 2,400 new
   conscripts with 71 \% of sensitivity and 58 \% of specificity. The
   cut-off points of less than 5.5 was recommended for HIV preventive
   purpose.},
