Note = {24th International Symposium on Research and Applications in Psychology
   (SICAP) - Cognitive Characteristics of Transdisciplinarity. Applications
   in Psychology and Psychotherapies, Timisoara, ROMANIA, MAR 24-26, 2017},
Abstract = {This research is concerned with analyzing youth usefulness perception on
   two core career counselling activities: professional interests and
   skills testing and receiving information about job openings, in order to
   delineate what triggers youth to be more committed to pursuing a
   specific career. The main purpose of current study is to analyze the
   relationship between youth professional self-schema (perceived
   professional interests and skills testing) and perceived usefulness of
   receiving job openings of 112 1st to 4th year students of the ``Aurel
   Vlaicu{''} University of Arad.
   The dynamic relationship identified, demonstrates that extreme scores on
   youth professional self-schema significantly influences the job
   searching behaviour pattern, in terms of perceiving as not useful
   information regarding job openings, while situating on the middle
   continuum between strong and weak professional self-schema, gives youth
   incentives for consider these type of information as useful and actually
   making them more open in applying for jobs.
   Conclusions and practical implications are discussed.},
