Note = {4th International Conference on Emotions and Organizational Life,
   Birkbeck Coll, London, ENGLAND, JUN, 2004},
Abstract = {Theory suggests that affective commitment and organizational citizenship
   behavior are positively correlated. Previous studies, however, report
   weak relationships between affective commitment and organizational
   citizenship behavior. The present study provides an interactive
   perspective in which we propose that emotional intelligence moderates
   the relationship between affective commitment and Organizational
   Citizenship Behaviors (OCBs) - altruism and compliance. We found
   significant interaction between emotional intelligence and affective
   commitment in predicting altruistic behavior. In other words, the
   positive relationship between affective commitment and OCB-altruism was
   stronger for high emotional intelligence individuals. Our prediction for
   compliance behavior was not supported.},
