   Environm; China Univ Geosciences; Univ S Australia, CRC CARE; China
   Assoc Sci \& Technol, China Ctr Int Sci \& Technol Exchange; OPCW},
Abstract = {The Irrigation District 005 is an agricultural territory in Chihuahua,
   Mexico where has been detected As in groundwater. So, the objective was
   to determine As in agricultural wells, and the metalloid traceability to
   soil and crops. 119 irrigation wells were sampled, 140 samples of soil,
   32 onion and 37 chili plants were collected. The As concentration was
   determined in all matrices by HG-AAS. 11\% of the wells exceeded the
   maximum permissible level (MPL) in Mexico of As in water for
   agricultural use (100 mu g L-1), the highest concentration was 576 mu g
   L-1. 13\% of the soil samples exceeded the MPL for agricultural use (22
   mg kg(-1)), the maximum concentration was 57.7 mg kg(-1). The highest As
   presence in crops was in root, 7.4 mg kg(-1) in chili and 28.8 mg kg(-1)
   in onion. However, 0.16 mg kg(-1) in chili crop and 0.38 mg kg(-1) in
   onion crop were also identified.},
