Abstract = {The potential for arsenite removal using plant-microbial fuel cells
   (PMFC) was evaluated. In such a system, O-2 is excreted by living rice
   plant roots and Fe(II) play important roles in initiating Fenton
   reactions. Fenton reagents, including H2O2, Fe(II), were generated
   in-situ without an electricity supply. The HO. produced in the Fenton
   reaction were capable of oxidizing arsenite apparently and efficiently.
   The results might provide a new insight for As(III) oxidation in rice
   rhizosphere.},
