   Assoc Sci \& Technol, China Ctr Int Sci \& Technol Exchange; OPCW},
Abstract = {The effects of inorganic arsenic on plants, the mechanisms involved in
   the uptake and transport of arsenic and how inorganic arsenic enters
   food chains are well documented. Regulatory limits have been established
   to control the inorganic arsenic concentrations in certain foods
   including rice. There is, however, a knowledge gap with respect to
   dimethylarsenic concentrations. In this study rice was grown
   hydroponically and exposed to varying DMA concentrations. High levels of
   DMA were detrimental to rice plants whereby plants showed symptoms
   consistent with Straighthead disease, a disease that results in dramatic
   yield losses.},
