Abstract = {Arsenic is considered a highly toxic metalloid, but the toxicity depends
   on its speciation. Inorganic species are considered more toxic than
   organic ones and the As(III) more toxic than As(V). This study evaluated
   the speciation of soluble arsenic after treatment of contaminated water
   by co-precipitation of Fe and Al (hydr)oxides. The results showed that
   the valence of Fe and presence of Al play an important role on As
