Abstract = {We conducted groundwater surveys in the Amazon Basin to determine the
   occurrence and distribution of arsenic and other contaminants. Initial
   results indicate that in groundwater resources in the recent floodplains
   of the Amazon River and of other white-water rivers, arsenic
   concentrations are often above the WHO-guideline value of 10 mu g L-1
   for drinking water. We compared the chemical analyses with geospatial
   data to identify vulnerable areas in the whole region. Understanding the
   regional geochemical mechanism(s) triggering the enrichment of arsenic
   in groundwater is important to raise awareness and implement mitigation
   where needed.},
