   Assoc Sci \& Technol, China Ctr Int Sci \& Technol Exchange; OPCW},
Abstract = {Nanoadsorbents have gained considerable attention for arsenic removal in
   groundwater among scientific communities from last decade.
   Nanotechnology based water treatment systems are logical choice in
   respect to resource and energy efficiency. The literature is widely
   replete in cases of development of different nanoadsorbents which are
   explored for arsenic removal. Among these, nanoscale zero-valent iron
   has been observed extensively employed both at laboratory and pilot
   scale studies due to its strong affinity, easy availability and
   environmental friendly nature. Its unstable nature limits the
   application at large scale efficiently. In present study, gamma-Fe2O3
   nanoparticles were evaluated for arsenic removal using Taguchi's design
   of experimental methodology for real world water conditions by
   formulating artificial groundwater.},
