Abstract = {The study is focused on locally-grown, such as carrots, beets and quinoa
   from the As-polluted Chiu Chiu area in Northern Chile. For the
   vegetables, were investigated: i) Their total As, Cu, Pb, Cr, Cd and Mn
   content ii) Arsenic speciation by LC-ICPMS analysis; iii) Arsenic
   bioaccessibility iv) Arsenic species present in the extracts and v)
   Arsenic dietary exposure. In vitro gastrointestinal digestion of As from
   carrots and beets, whereas efficiency was about 40\% for quinoa. For
   carrots, only As(III) and As(V) species were found, being their
   concentration levels similar. In the case of quinoa, around 85\% of the
   element was present as As(V).},
