Abstract = {Arsenic pollution is naturally present in groundwater and soils of the
   main agriculture production area of Argentine. Arsenic in soils, can be
   taken up and bioaccumulated in plant, and may be bio-transferred to
   agri-food and humans. All samples collected shown values between 18.6
   and 33.1 mg kg(-1) of total As. Range percentage of organic matter in
   analyzed samples were from 6.7 to 24.9\%. No significant correlation (p
   > 0.05) between total As level and organic matter was found. The As
   concentration in the analyzed samples were above the limits considered
   in Argentine. However, all samples were into the range previously
   reported by other authors.},
