   Technol HOME Program; Malardalen Univ, Future Energy Profile},
Abstract = {Low carbon energy (LCE) systems have played an essential role in
   minimizing building energy usage and carbon emissions. Early
   considerations of feasibility and integration for different types of LCE
   systems are beneficial for the building design process. In this study,
   an office building located in London was taken as an example, in which
   seven potential low carbon energy solutions were analysed qualitatively
   based on the `RESET' tool provided by CIBSE. Four feasible options were
   narrowed down including: solar thermal, photovoltaics, ground source
   heat pump (GSHP) and combined heat and power (CHP) systems. `RETScreen4'
   was then used to perform a quantitative analysis to select the
   appropriate solution. The results indicate that the CHP system gave the
   best performance environmentally and economically with the relevant
   assumptions. (C) 2016 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
