Organization = {AMER CHEM SOC, DIV NUCL CHEM \& TECHNOL; AMER CHEM SOC, DIV CHEM HLTH \&
   SAFETY; AMER CHEM SOC, DIV ENVIRONM CHEM INC},
Abstract = {Although the study of mental retardation among children exposed to
   atomic radiation in utero has clearly shown an effect of exposure on the
   developing brain, the cancer risk among these individuals remains to be
   determined and will only be established through continued follow-up of
   the subjects. To this end mortality and morbidity surveys of about 1800
   persons exposed in utero to the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and
   Nagasaki were undertaken at the Radiation Effects Research Foundation
   (RERF). In the years 1950-1984, when these individuals were under the
   age of 40, a significant excess cancer risk was observed. The relative
   risk at 1 Gy was about 3.8. However, in the most recent 5 years
   (1985-1989), there was no apparent excess of cancer, and the overall
   relative risk for the years 1950-1989 decreased to about two based on
   the 2 dozen cancer cases with DS86 dose estimates that have been seen
   thus far.},
