Abstract = {Marine disasters are a more prevalent problem in China than in many
   other countries. Based on the development of a status quo of China's
   marine disaster the space-time process model is used. The model uses the
   ocean's temperature field, salinity field, water density field, surface
   wind field, wave field and other four-dimensional spatio-temporal
   quantities. This paper studies that model in detail. This study aims at
   using the theory to provide support during marine disasters in an effort
   to prevent or decrease their frequency in the future.},
