Note = {IWA 11th Micropol and Ecohazard Conference, Seoul, SOUTH KOREA, OCT
   20-24, 2019},
Organization = {IWA},
Abstract = {This study analyzed residues of PPCPs in secondary treated sewage water,
   and their amount eliminated by ozonation processes. A microbubble nozzle
   and ejector were used to dissolve ozone. To consider a low concentration
   of PPCPs, a SPE method was performed on samples prior to the analysis.
   The concentration of dissolved ozone was 4.00 mg/L in the microbubble
   and 2.49 mg/L in the ejector. To examine elimination trends, the
   experiment was also performed at a low concentration of ozone, 1/10 of
   its original concentration. The maximum elimination rate on average was
   93.0\% in the ejector, higher than that in the microbubble (90.1\%), but
   16 PPCPs were found to show a relatively high elimination rate in the
   microbubble, higher than the ejector. Elimination trends with respect to
   time were distinguished based on inflection point, and 11 PPCPs were
   concentrated on the latter half of the microbubble after the inflection
   point at the low concentration of ozone, which was compared to other
   cases. In the source water, concentrations of 2 PPCPs were higher than
   the reference toxic concentration based on the QSAR model, but after
   treatment, only bezafibrate was over the value when the ejector with low
   ozone injection concentration was applied.},
